URL:https://citp.princeton.edu/events/2026/arvind-narayanan-ai-agents-and-a
 ugmentation-agenda
LOCATION:Sherrerd Hall 306
SUMMARY:Arvind Narayanan - AI Agents and the Augmentation Agenda
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:The dominant paradigm in AI research and development envisions 
 the goal as automation of tasks and entire jobs. But another\, comparative
 ly marginalized vision has existed since the beginning of AI — that of a
 ugmenting workers and amplifying human potential. In this talk\, it is arg
 ued that the automation agenda is struggling even on purely commercial gro
 unds\, and it is time to invest more into augmentation. Building agents fo
 r collaboration instead of automation requires elevating a set of underexp
 lored research challenges in human-computer interaction. Such agents can b
 etter serve human
CATEGORIES:Artificial Intelligence, Data Science & Society
