URL:https://citp.princeton.edu/events/2026/joshua-cohen-dark-mansions-ai-in
 novation-and-fermat%E2%80%99s-last-theorem
LOCATION:Computer Science Building 105
SUMMARY:Joshua Cohen - DARK MANSIONS: AI\, Innovation\, and Fermat’s Last
  Theorem
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Yiu\, Kosoy\, and Gopnik (2024) argue that “Cultural evolutio
 n depends on a fine balance between imitation and innovation.” Writing i
 n a world prior to reasoning models\, they argued that large language mode
 ls fall squarely on the imitation side. This paper—focused principally o
 n formal and scientific innovation—proposes a finer-grained\, three-tier
  taxonomy: Tier 1 is transmission\, Tier 2 is something new (invention) wi
 thin a fixed problem formulation\, and Tier 3 is framework-generating inno
 vation. Tier 3 requires both historical novelty—a new construction or fr
 amework—and functional novelty—a
CATEGORIES:Artificial Intelligence, Data Science & Society
